#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Film the background agent (Hermes) doing real jobs for a person.

A separate recording from the desktop tour (tools/demo/umoja-demo, whose
machinery it reuses: the same safety checks, clips, captions, GIFs and
trailer). Run it from a terminal inside an Umoja session with the
background agent set up (Ask Umoja's settings, Background agent, Set Up),
then keep your hands off the keyboard and mouse. Each job is handed over the
way a person would, by typing "@agent ..." into Ask Umoja, and is real: the
agent runs on your model (local, cloud, or both with "Use the cloud model
for harder requests") and writes real files.

    tools/demo/umoja-agent-demo                    # every scene, into docs/agent-demo
    tools/demo/umoja-agent-demo --only agent-tidy agent-budget
    tools/demo/umoja-agent-demo --suspend          # also film "close the lid"

The scenes:

    agent-intro    where it lives: Ask Umoja's settings and the Agents button
    agent-trip     "plan a weekend in Lisbon": a day-by-day plan with a budget
    agent-weather  the guardrails: it asks before reaching a new site
                   (wttr.in), you Allow, and the forecast lands in the plan
    agent-tidy     a messy Downloads folder, shared with it, sorted into
                   folders, with a note of what it moved
    agent-budget   a bank export, shared read-only, turned into a budget
                   summary with subscriptions worth cancelling
    agent-lid      (--suspend) close the lid mid-job: it carries on after
                   the laptop wakes (sudo -n rtcwake, 25 s)
    agent-wrap     everything it made, in ~/Agents/<Name>

The demo's own files (the Downloads and Finances folders) live in
~/Umoja Agent Demo and are removed at the end, shares included. What the
agent wrote stays in ~/Agents/<Name>; files from an earlier run with the
same names are moved aside first so every run starts clean.

Nothing is installed or sent anywhere except what the jobs need: the model,
and wttr.in once you'd Allow it (the scene does, on camera).
"""

